{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:95b230a4151c488b","name":"Vehicle Battalion","source":{"id":"source:reference-95b230a4151c488b","title":"Vehicle Battalion","revision":20089,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:11:09Z","sha256":"a67f83daef21a16ad6e6358307d4b7a76f614233181f4d1537658c0dcb20b3aa","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20089","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Vehicle%20Battalion&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-95b230a4151c488b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Wars Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Wars_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Large, Huge, and Gargantuan ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," can also be combined into ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},". A Vehicle Battalion typically represents four of the same ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},". To create a Vehicle Battalion, multiply the Vehicle's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"}," by 4 and calculate ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attrition"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attrition"}," numbers based on the new Hit Point total.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Like normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},", Vehicle Battalions take half damage from all non-",{"tag":"a","children":["Area Attacks"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Area_Attacks"},", but also suffer ",{"tag":"a","children":["Persistent Conditions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Persistent_Conditions"}," due to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Attrition"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Attrition"},", as per normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion"}," rules. Additionally, if a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," possesses any antipersonnel weapon (weapons that do not have a damage multiplier), the damage is for those ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"}," also gains the x2 damage multiplier for the Vehicle Battalion. Otherwise, Vehicles follow all the same rules for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},". Additionally, Vehicle Battalions can take ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Actions?action=edit&redlink=1"}," as though they were individual ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeders","referenceId":"reference:8831ac17fd67f6fc"}," can also join together into ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fighter Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fighter_Groups","referenceId":"reference:69e9c1663668ad68"}," instead of forming a Battalion, following the normal rules for ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fighter Groups"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fighter_Groups","referenceId":"reference:69e9c1663668ad68"},". ",{"tag":"a","children":["Colossal Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Colossal_Vehicles","referenceId":"reference:8637d2579a61284c"}," typically operate alone in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"},". Colossal (Frigate) and larger ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," are typically used as terrain elements, and are usually not a part of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mass Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mass_Combat"}," (except when they perform ",{"tag":"a","children":["Orbital Bombardment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Orbital_Bombardment"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Vehicle Battalions do not have the same ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalion Positions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalion_Positions"}," as normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Battalions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Battalions"},". Instead, the Vehicle Battalion is considered to have the same ",{"tag":"a","children":["Crew Positions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Crew_Positions"}," as in normal ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Combat"},", as determined by the base ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},". If a unique character occupies a role in a Vehicle Battalion, use the lower of the unique character's statistics and the default statistics for that Battalion's role. For example, if a hero with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," of +10 acts as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Gunner"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Gunner","referenceId":"reference:0cbc0bc5729f801f"}," on a Vehicle Battalion with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Base Attack Bonus"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Base_Attack_Bonus"}," of +4, that Vehicle Battalion still uses the +4 from the Vehicle Battalion's base statistics.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
